\description{
Complete an admin-shares table to the full year range of its extent and
fill the pre-seam years by modulating each unit's seam-year share with
its own land extent, the plan's decision-7 back-cast:

\deqn{\tilde{s}_u(t) = s_u(t_0) \frac{E_u(t)}{E_u(t_0)}, \qquad
      s_u(t) = \frac{\tilde{s}_u(t)}{\sum_v \tilde{s}_v(t)}}

The first step is \code{\link[=fill_proxy_growth]{fill_proxy_growth()}} with the extent as proxy, the
same machinery \code{.fill_pre_faostat()} (\code{R/build_production.R:3008}) uses
to back-cast the national totals these shares split, so the two
compose. The second is a per-year renormalisation over the \code{t0} unit
set, the residual pseudo-unit included when the shares carry one.

Nothing here is a fallback: a year the rules cannot resolve is refused
with a diagnostic and keeps \code{share = NA}, never a carried value.

Two things the plan's seam section names are deliberately \strong{not} here.
Pre-seam irrigation needs no separate treatment: the unit irrigated
target is built from the engine's own annual \code{ir_potential}
(\code{R/spatialize.R:420}), whose LUH2 \code{irrigated_ha} varies every year,
pre-seam years included, so it moves with the same extent that
modulates the area share. And the within-unit weight \emph{regime} per
\verb{(unit, item, year)} is the allocation's to record, not this
function's: \code{treatment} here says how a share was obtained, while the
regime says which weight then spread it inside the unit.
